Checkout discount logic; harden the suite until the listed mutants all fail. Save /workspace/promo.js:

function promoDiscountCents(subtotalCents, isFirstOrder, itemCount) {
  let discount = 0;
  if (isFirstOrder) {
    discount = Math.min(1500, Math.round(subtotalCents * 0.15));
  }
  if (itemCount >= 5) {
    discount += 500;
  }
  if (discount > subtotalCents) {
    discount = subtotalCents;
  }
  return discount;
}
module.exports = { promoDiscountCents };

Seed tests (create promo.test.js, node:test, require syntax): one case promoDiscountCents(10000, true, 1) === 1500 and one promoDiscountCents(10000, false, 1) === 0. Mutants to kill: M1: 0.15 -> 0.05. M2: Math.min -> Math.max. M3: >= 5 -> > 5. M4: += 500 -> = 500. M5: discount > subtotalCents -> discount >= subtotalCents (careful: is this one even observable? argue it in a comment, and if truly equivalent swap in the alternative mutant discount > subtotalCents -> discount < subtotalCents). M6: Math.round -> Math.floor. Craft cases: subtotal where 15% exceeds the 1500 cap and where it does not (kills M1/M2), itemCount exactly 5 and 4 (M3), first order AND 5 items so stacking matters (M4), a subtotal of 9 with 15% rounding to 1 (Math.round(1.35)=1) versus a subtotal like 30 where round vs floor differ on 4.5 (M6), and a tiny subtotal where the clamp engages (M5-alt). Verify via a node mutation-harness script string-replacing each mutant into a temp copy and running its tests; print the KILLED table, 6/6 required, pristine suite green.

